  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting ready for a new kitchen backsplash is exciting, and a little planning goes a long way to making sure everything runs smoothly! First off, you'll want to accurately measure the area you're tiling. Then, take some time to plan out your tile layout — this helps avoid awkward cuts and makes sure the pattern looks great. Before you even think about thinset, protect your countertops and cabinets; nobody wants grout on their new surfaces. Don't forget to turn off the power to any outlets and remove the covers so you can work safely. Prepping the wall is super important; sometimes you might need repairs or a backer board for a solid foundation. After all that, you're ready to start setting your tile, then grouting and sealing after it's had enough time to cure. Remember, those cure times are really important, so don't rush them! If your walls aren't perfectly flat or if you're dealing with complex patterns or lighting, it's smart to call in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC. We can handle the trickier parts and ensure a clean, professional finish, especially around outlets and edges."
    }
  ],
